<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  TC8 §4.2.4.1 ARP_35 negative — lwIP ingress-fault self-validation of the positive's
  absent-entry guard. The trait arms kArpFaultIgnoreLearn and sends the positive's
  gratuitous Response followed by its teaching Request. The hook is opcode-1 gated, so
  it swallows the Request; on this fixture that is the only teaching that would have
  landed, because lwIP's etharp creates no entry from a gratuitous Response (the
  mechanism ARP_06's known-fail records). The DUT therefore holds no entry and emits
  the opcode-1 ARP Request the positive's `dut_arp_request_after_double_injection`
  final forbids. Pass = that Request; fail_compliant = none within the window, meaning
  the DUT resolved from cache anyway and the fault was inert.

  ARP_35 has no stale-MAC sibling for the same reason: with no first entry to keep,
  kArpFaultIgnoreUpdate would find nothing already held and swallow nothing.

  lwIP-only (kCapIngressFault + kCapArpConditioning). Envelope: arp_cache_staleness_neg.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       xmlns:cpp="urn:sce:cpp"
       version="1.0"
       name="arp_35_neg"
       datamodel="null"
       initial="listening">
  <sce:use template="../_templates/arp_cache_staleness_neg.sce-template.xml"/>
</scxml>
